---
description: Standard module structure following Clean Architecture pattern with domain, application, and infrastructure layers
globs: src/**/*.module.ts, src/**/index.ts, src/**/application/**/*, src/**/infrastructure/**/*, src/**/domain/**/*
alwaysApply: true
---

- **Module Structure Overview**
  - All modules must follow the Clean Architecture pattern with three main layers: `domain`, `application`, and `infrastructure`
  - Reference implementation: [user module](mdc:src/user)
  - Each module should be self-contained with proper separation of concerns

- **Root Level Structure**
  - **Required Files:**
    - `index.ts` - Main export file that re-exports from all layers
    - `{module-name}.module.ts` - NestJS module definition
  - **Example from [user/index.ts](mdc:src/user/index.ts):**
  ```typescript
  export * from './domain';
  export * from './application';
  export * from './infrastructure';
  export * from './user.module';
  ```

- **Domain Layer (`domain/`)**
  - **Purpose:** Contains business logic, entities, enums, and repository interfaces
  - **Required Structure:**
    - `entities/` - Domain entities (business objects)
      - `{entity-name}.entity.ts` - Entity class
      - `index.ts` - Export all entities
    - `enums/` - Domain enumerations
      - `{enum-name}.enum.ts` - Enum definition
      - `index.ts` - Export all enums
    - `repositories/` - Repository interfaces (contracts)
      - `{entity-name}.repository.interface.ts` - Interface definition
      - `index.ts` - Export all repository interfaces
    - `index.ts` - Export from entities, enums, and repositories
  - **Example from [user/domain/index.ts](mdc:src/user/domain/index.ts):**
  ```typescript
  export * from './entities';
  export * from './enums';
  export * from './repositories';
  ```
  - **Rules:**
    - ✅ DO: Keep domain layer pure (no framework dependencies)
    - ✅ DO: Use interfaces for repositories (dependency inversion)
    - ❌ DON'T: Import from infrastructure or application layers
    - ❌ DON'T: Include NestJS decorators in domain entities

- **Application Layer (`application/`)**
  - **Purpose:** Contains use cases and business logic orchestration
  - **Required Structure:**
    - `{module-name}.service.ts` - Main service class with business logic
    - `index.ts` - Export the service
  - **Example from [user/application/user.service.ts](mdc:src/user/application/user.service.ts):**
  ```typescript
  import { Injectable, Inject } from '@nestjs/common';
  import { User } from '../domain/entities';
  import type { IUserRepository } from '../domain/repositories';
  import { USER_REPOSITORY } from '../infrastructure/user.constants';

  @Injectable()
  export class UserService {
    constructor(
      @Inject(USER_REPOSITORY)
      private readonly userRepository: IUserRepository,
    ) {}
    // ... methods
  }
  ```
  - **Rules:**
    - ✅ DO: Inject repository interfaces using constants from infrastructure
    - ✅ DO: Use `type` import for interfaces to avoid runtime dependencies
    - ✅ DO: Keep services focused on business logic
    - ❌ DON'T: Import directly from infrastructure implementations
    - ❌ DON'T: Include HTTP-specific logic (that belongs in controllers)

- **Infrastructure Layer (`infrastructure/`)**
  - **Purpose:** Contains framework-specific implementations, controllers, DTOs, and external integrations
  - **Required Structure:**
    - `controllers/` - HTTP controllers
      - `{module-name}.controller.ts` - Controller class
      - `index.ts` - Export controller
    - `dto/` - Data Transfer Objects for API requests/responses
      - `{action}-{entity}.dto.ts` - DTO classes (e.g., `create-user.dto.ts`)
      - `index.ts` - Export all DTOs
    - `repositories/` - Repository implementations
      - `prisma-{entity}.repository.ts` - Prisma implementation
      - `index.ts` - Export repository implementation
    - `{module-name}.constants.ts` - Dependency injection tokens
    - `index.ts` - Export from controllers, dto, repositories, and constants
  - **Example from [user/infrastructure/index.ts](mdc:src/user/infrastructure/index.ts):**
  ```typescript
  export * from './controllers';
  export * from './dto';
  export * from './repositories';
  export * from './user.constants';
  ```
  - **Constants Pattern from [user/infrastructure/user.constants.ts](mdc:src/user/infrastructure/user.constants.ts):**
  ```typescript
  export const USER_REPOSITORY = 'USER_REPOSITORY';
  ```
  - **Rules:**
    - ✅ DO: Use Prisma for database implementations
    - ✅ DO: Create constants file for DI tokens (follow `{MODULE}_REPOSITORY` pattern)
    - ✅ DO: Keep controllers thin (delegate to services)
    - ✅ DO: Use DTOs for all API inputs/outputs
    - ❌ DON'T: Put business logic in controllers
    - ❌ DON'T: Import domain entities directly in DTOs (use separate DTOs)

- **Module Definition Pattern**
  - **Example from [user/user.module.ts](mdc:src/user/user.module.ts):**
  ```typescript
  import { Module } from '@nestjs/common';
  import { UserService } from './application/user.service';
  import { UserController } from './infrastructure/controllers';
  import { PrismaUserRepository } from './infrastructure/repositories';
  import { USER_REPOSITORY } from './infrastructure/user.constants';
  import { PrismaModule } from '../prisma/prisma.module';

  @Module({
    imports: [PrismaModule],
    controllers: [UserController],
    providers: [
      UserService,
      {
        provide: USER_REPOSITORY,
        useClass: PrismaUserRepository,
      },
    ],
    exports: [UserService],
  })
  export class UserModule {}
  ```
  - **Rules:**
    - ✅ DO: Import PrismaModule for database access
    - ✅ DO: Use provider pattern with constants for repository injection
    - ✅ DO: Export services that other modules might need
    - ✅ DO: Register controllers from infrastructure layer
    - ❌ DON'T: Import domain entities directly in module
    - ❌ DON'T: Export repository implementations (only interfaces via services)

- **Index Files Pattern**
  - Every directory should have an `index.ts` that re-exports its contents
  - This enables clean imports: `from './domain'` instead of `from './domain/entities/user.entity'`
  - **Example pattern:**
  ```typescript
  // In subdirectories (entities/, enums/, etc.)
  export * from './user.entity';
  
  // In layer directories (domain/, application/, infrastructure/)
  export * from './entities';
  export * from './enums';
  ```

- **Naming Conventions**
  - Module folder: `{module-name}/` (lowercase, kebab-case if multi-word)
  - Module class: `{ModuleName}Module` (PascalCase)
  - Service: `{ModuleName}Service` (PascalCase)
  - Controller: `{ModuleName}Controller` (PascalCase)
  - Entity: `{EntityName}` (PascalCase)
  - Repository interface: `I{EntityName}Repository` (PascalCase with I prefix)
  - Repository implementation: `Prisma{EntityName}Repository` (PascalCase)
  - Constants: `{MODULE}_REPOSITORY` (UPPER_SNAKE_CASE)
  - DTOs: `{Action}{Entity}Dto` (PascalCase, e.g., `CreateUserDto`)

- **Dependency Direction**
  - Domain ← Application ← Infrastructure
  - Domain should have zero dependencies
  - Application depends only on Domain
  - Infrastructure depends on Domain and Application
  - Never reverse these dependencies

- **When Creating a New Module**
  1. Create root folder: `src/{module-name}/`
  2. Create three layer folders: `domain/`, `application/`, `infrastructure/`
  3. Set up domain layer: entities, enums, repository interfaces
  4. Set up application layer: service class
  5. Set up infrastructure layer: controller, DTOs, repository implementation, constants
  6. Create all `index.ts` files for proper exports
  7. Create `{module-name}.module.ts` with proper NestJS configuration
  8. Create root `index.ts` exporting all layers
  9. Follow the exact structure from [user module](mdc:src/user) as reference
